Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; python-wheels does not open issues/PRs on third-party repos]

Add riscv64-linux vcpkg overlay triplets mirroring the arm64-linux ones.

setup.py points VCPKG_OVERLAY_TRIPLETS at cmake/triplets/release, which only
carries x64/arm64 triplets. On a riscv64 host vcpkg then falls back to its
community riscv64-linux triplet, which builds every port in both debug and
release and links libusb/ffmpeg statically, unlike every other Linux wheel.
These are the arm64-linux triplets with the architecture changed and vcpkg's
default ELF RPATH fixup turned off for the static ports: riscv64 links non-PIE
executables at 0x10000, which is vm.mmap_min_addr, and patchelf's
--set-rpath on such an executable maps a new first LOAD segment below it, so
the patched pkgconf segfaults on exec when ffmpeg's portfile runs it.

diff --git a/cmake/triplets/release/riscv64-linux.cmake b/cmake/triplets/release/riscv64-linux.cmake
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3613a45
--- /dev/null
+++ b/cmake/triplets/release/riscv64-linux.cmake
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+set(VCPKG_TARGET_ARCHITECTURE riscv64)
+set(VCPKG_CRT_LINKAGE dynamic)
+set(VCPKG_LIBRARY_LINKAGE static)
+set(VCPKG_BUILD_TYPE release)
+
+set(PORT_DEBUG ON)
+
+if(PORT MATCHES "libusb|ffmpeg")
+    set(VCPKG_LIBRARY_LINKAGE dynamic)
+    set(VCPKG_FIXUP_ELF_RPATH ON)
+else()
+    # patchelf moves a non-PIE executable's first LOAD segment below riscv64's 0x10000 base,
+    # i.e. below vm.mmap_min_addr, so every vcpkg-built tool (pkgconf, protoc) segfaults on exec
+    set(VCPKG_FIXUP_ELF_RPATH OFF)
+endif()
+if(PORT MATCHES "vulkan-loader")
+    # When building in GH Actions environment, vcpkg's pkg-conf can't find XCB/X11 libraries
+    set(VCPKG_CMAKE_CONFIGURE_OPTIONS "-DPKG_CONFIG_EXECUTABLE=/usr/bin/pkg-config")
+
+endif()
+
+set(VCPKG_CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME Linux)
